 "callout": "<b>Why this sits alongside the GA4 dashboard.</b> Covers came in at <b>12,191</b>, <b>up 6.3 per cent</b> week on week against a freshly recomputed prior week of 11,469, and the highest of the eight weeks on record. Website is <b>56 per cent</b> of London covers; OpenTable, Google Reserve, walk-ins and the rest never reach the GA4 number. Year on year the portfolio reads <b>up 56 per cent</b>, but <b>DSL</b> was closed for its rebrand in the matched 2025 week and contributes 3,331 covers against nothing last year: <b>ex DSL the figure is up 13.7 per cent</b>. Bookable covers, meaning website plus OpenTable plus Google Reserve, were <b>9,333</b>, up 4.2 per cent on the week and up 10.1 per cent on last year ex DSL. The bulk-import rule removed 105 covers from 39 OpenTable bookings, 82 covers at DSL, 20 at Azzurra and 3 at Aqua Shard. Read the GA4 dashboard as the website channel and this report as demand: four of the six GA4 properties under-recorded all week while covers rose."
